<% content_for :page_title,"Native Studio Workstation" %>
<%= stylesheet_link_tag "/lightek/workstation.css" %>
<%= javascript_include_tag "/lightek/workstation.js",defer:true %>
<main class="sw-page" data-studio-workstation data-status-url="<%= status_dashboard_studio_workstation_path(@session.session_key) %>" data-ticket-url="<%= ticket_dashboard_studio_workstation_path(@session.session_key) %>" data-save-url="<%= save_dashboard_studio_workstation_path(@session.session_key) %>" data-workspace-url="<%= workspace_dashboard_studio_workstation_path(@session.session_key) %>" data-stop-url="<%= dashboard_studio_workstation_path(@session.session_key) %>">
  <header><div><span>LIGHTEK MEDIA OS / NATIVE AUTHORING</span><h1><%= @scene.name %></h1><p>Full Blender editors inside your Studio workspace. Your source, rigs, nodes, simulation settings and animation remain native.</p></div><a href="/lightek/index.html#/studio/<%= @scene.id %>">Back to production</a></header>
  <nav class="sw-toolbar" aria-label="Native workstation controls"><button type="button" data-connect>Connect editor</button><button type="button" class="sw-primary" data-save>Save version to Studio</button><button type="button" data-fullscreen>Full screen</button><button type="button" data-stop>Close workstation</button><span role="status" aria-live="polite" data-status>Preparing native workstation…</span></nav>
  <p role="alert" data-error hidden></p>
  <div class="sw-layout"><section class="sw-screen" aria-label="Native Blender editor"><div data-placeholder><h2>Your production workstation</h2><p>Studio is preparing an isolated Blender session from this saved scene. The original project and asset stay unchanged.</p></div><iframe title="Native Blender production workstation" data-desktop hidden referrerpolicy="no-referrer" allow="fullscreen; clipboard-read; clipboard-write"></iframe></section>
  <aside><h2>Production guide</h2><div class="sw-tasks" aria-label="Production workspaces"><% {"layout"=>"Layout", "model"=>"Modeling", "sculpt"=>"Sculpting", "uv"=>"UV Editing", "animate"=>"Animation & rigging", "shade"=>"Shading", "geometry"=>"Geometry Nodes", "composite"=>"Compositing", "sequence"=>"Sequence editor", "render"=>"Rendering"}.each do |task,label| %><button type="button" data-workspace="<%= task %>"><%= label %></button><% end %></div><p>Use the workspaces across the top of Blender to change the editing task. Imported project layouts stay available.</p><dl><dt>Layout / Modeling</dt><dd>Select objects; Tab changes mesh mode. G, R and S move, rotate and scale.</dd><dt>Sculpting</dt><dd>Use Blender’s sculpt brushes, masks, symmetry, remeshing and detail controls.</dd><dt>UV Editing / Texture Paint</dt><dd>Unwrap, mark seams, edit UVs and paint the native project’s textures.</dd><dt>Rigging / Animation</dt><dd>Use Pose mode, constraints, bone controls, Dope Sheet, Graph Editor and NLA.</dd><dt>Shading / Geometry Nodes</dt><dd>Edit the complete native graphs, groups, sockets and node properties.</dd><dt>Physics / Simulation</dt><dd>Configure and bake effects inside this session. Keep cache files under /work so Studio can retain them.</dd><dt>Compositing / Video Editing</dt><dd>Work with Blender’s compositor and sequence editor, then save back to Studio.</dd></dl><p><b>Save version to Studio</b> triggers Blender’s trusted save bridge, imports a new Library asset and opens a separate editable production. Source credits follow it. Close modal dialogs before saving.</p><a data-saved-project hidden>Open saved production</a><a data-saved-library hidden href="/lightek/index.html#/studio/library">Open asset library</a><p>Use Studio’s movie export and timeline for publication, or prepare a GLB stage for Live Studio. This editor session lasts up to four hours. Closing the tab does not publish or broadcast.</p></aside></div>
</main>
